From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 16:46:18 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 680/687] perf(dspark): capture context graphs at the target's decode
 graph sizes

DSparkContextCudaGraphs captured powers of two plus the limit, so a
full-depth decode step (1 + 5 rows a request) padded 6 -> 8, 24 -> 32
and 48 -> 64 rows through main_proj (and its TP all_gather), main_norm
and the three draft layers' KV projection, norm, RoPE and cache write.
The context graph runs at the target step's live row count; capture
the row counts of the target's own FULL decode graphs instead: the
compilation config's capture ladder and the token totals of
dense_varlen_decode_shapes (every one- and two-request total, every
full-depth step) at one request's verification width, up to the
context limit, which stays captured.

Base: candidate-37 patch head 5b7cfa37 (local-inference-lab/vllm
19f2c20e plus the series). Supersedes the unmerged ladder of the
2026-10-31 dspark-context-cudagraph-ladder experiment, which kept
powers of two and its own copy of the decode shapes.

Quality: none. The context rows are the same; padded rows past the
step remain PAD-slotted and are never written to the cache. No new
kernel shape: every size is a row count the declared row tiles serve.

Graphs: the target's decode graph count below the limit, 23 at
tp3-triangle (was 7) and 35 at tp4-ring (was 8), in the shared graph
pool.

Tests: tests/kernels/test_deepseek_v41_tilelang_dspark_context.py
checks the sizes against a target CudaGraphManager planned as the
model runner plans it (tp3-triangle, tp4-ring, copy-draft width), and
that every decode step the target runs as a FULL graph replays a
context graph no wider than the target's.

Upstream: local; DSpark V4.1 is not in vllm-project/vllm.
